--- body ---
## Context
The merge gate (ticket 1045, closed 2026-10-21) makes `main` move only by a gate record, journals every
update of `main`, and audits the last 24 hours from lair. All of it rests on the forge ruleset
`main-traceability` (deletion and non-fast-forward refused, empty bypass list) staying as set.
Today the forge login that agent sessions use is the author's own owner account, so a session can edit
the ruleset, repository settings and Actions. A session did on 2026-10-06 at the author's request, and on
2026-10-21 the author delegated settings administration to the agent ("I trust you to admin my GH").
The gate leaves no open door only if no routine session credential can reopen one.

This is a forge setting, the author's act. It is not an agent task: an agent cannot remove rights from
the login it runs under.

## Decision for the author
Pick one, then record it here.
1. A separate agent identity or fine-grained token for sessions: contents and pull requests read/write,
   issues read, checks read; no administration, no workflow or Actions write. The owner account stays
   for the author's own admin acts.
2. Keep the owner login and accept the open door, writing that down as a decision (the gate then rests
   on discipline plus the audit, not on the forge).
3. A deploy-style hybrid: sessions use option 1, and a delegated admin token is issued for one session
   at a time on request and revoked after.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The author's choice is recorded in this ticket's log.
- [ ] If option 1 or 3: sessions run with the narrow credential, and `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/rulesets`
      with that credential answers 403 for a write (a GET may succeed), verified by the author or by a
      session running that one call with a throwaway ruleset-edit attempt that is expected to fail.
- [ ] The permissions census (`scripts/census/permissions.py`) and `conception/local-merge-gate-policy.md`
      state which credential sessions use, in one place.
- [ ] Merge, branch push and PR creation still work for sessions with the narrow credential (the merge
      recipe `skills/merge/SKILL.md` runs end to end once on it).
- [ ] Nothing here requires a particular agent runtime.

## Notes
- Do not hand an agent a broader token to "set this up": the author creates the token.
- Never put the token in a repository file or in a conversation; the harness guards forbid displaying it.
- Related: ticket 1180 (guard enforce, the author's other open act), conception/local-merge-gate-policy.md.
